# GEMINI_API_KEY: Required for Gemini AI API calls.
# This is a placeholder key.
# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime from user secrets.
# Users configure this via the Secrets panel in the AI Studio UI.
# IMPORTANT: Uncomment the line below if your app uses the Gemini API.
# If left commented out, the key will NOT be packaged in the APK.
# GEMINI_API_KEY=MY_GEMINI_API_KEY

# Public Client Build Configuration (NON-SECRET — do NOT put these as secrets in .env.example,
# supply via Gradle properties `-P...` or CI environment variables instead):
# - AGT_RUNTIME_MANIFEST_URL (or AGT_RUNTIME_MANIFEST_URL_DEV for debug builds)
# - AGT_GITHUB_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID (or AGT_GITHUB_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID_DEV for debug builds)
#
# SECURITY: Never define or embed a GitHub OAuth Client Secret (GITHUB_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET) in the APK.
# GitHub login uses Authorization Code Flow with PKCE (public client).

